          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The learned advocate relies on Section 222 of the Code of Criminal Procedure, which is reproduced herein below:-\n\"222."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "c9aae740972847e9a55619cb8aba3cfb_11",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "When offence proved included in offence charged.--(1) When a person is charged with an offence consisting of several particulars, a combination of some only of which constitutes a complete minor offence, and such combination is proved, but "
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "5994ee1f2d4a45e7953a2a6d66a5e80d_12",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n(2) When a person is charged with an offence and facts are proved which reduce it to a minor offence, he may be convicted of the minor offence, although he is not charged with it."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "fa94274c9e2547f6926029d09707e4f9_13",
